Figure~\ref{fig:overview} gives an overview of the pipeline. Four models are formed from two encoders (PhoBERT, BamiBERT) and two classification models (CNN, BiLSTM); all other factors---data, splits, input content, seed, optimization parameters, and number of epochs---are kept constant, so that differences in results stem solely from the encoders and classification models.

\subsection{Data Collection}
The dataset consists of information technology articles collected from six Vietnamese news sites: ICTnews (VietNamNet), Quan Tri Mang, Thanh Nien, VnExpress, GenK, and Tuoi Tre. It contains three text types: \textbf{Human} (original articles from human authors written by human authors), \textbf{AI-Generated} (articles generated from scratch by an LLM from a prompt by giving a topic and asking for a human-like writing styles), and \textbf{AI-Rewritten} (original articles rewritten by an LLM).

The AI texts were produced with two LLMs, Gemini (Google) and DeepSeek, through their free chat interfaces; since the free versions may change over time, I cannot identify the exact model versions. The two AI types are labeled 1 and the human articles 0, giving a balanced dataset of 2,500 human-written, 1,250 AI-generated, and 1,250 AI-rewritten articles (Table~\ref{tab:dataset}). The dataset is publicly available at: \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/DeckardLong/ai-content-detection-dataset}.

